<title>SLOVENIA: Adria passenger numbers up six pct in first half.</title>
<headline>Adria passenger numbers up six pct in first half.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia's state-owned Adria Airways said on Friday it carried 270,000 passengers in the first six months of this year, up six percent from the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>The country's sole carrier said traffic on scheduled flights firmed by one percent, while the number of passengers on charter lines jumped 18 percent.</p>
<p>Cargo traffic rose three percent to 1,900 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
</text>
